<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive launcher icon (API 26+).

  Built from the user-supplied artwork: a dark-ink planet with a glowing Q, a star ring and two
  small bodies. The source image carried a "豆包AI生成" watermark in its bottom-right corner; it was
  cropped out before any density was generated, so no launcher size can show it.

  Three layers, each with a reason:

  - background = Paper (#F7F6F2), NOT a saturated brand colour. The artwork is monochrome
    dark-ink-on-light, so a coloured plate would fight it and make the planet read as a sticker.
    Paper is also the app's own page colour, so the icon and the app look like the same product.
  - foreground = the artwork scaled into the inner 66dp safe zone of the 108dp canvas. Anything
    outside that zone is where launchers apply their mask, and the star ring reaches the edge of
    the art — drawing it full-bleed would let an aggressive circular mask slice the ring off.
  - monochrome = an alpha-only silhouette of the same shape, for Android 13+ themed icons. The
    system tints it, so its RGB is irrelevant; only the alpha matters.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
